abstract: >-
  Archival release of the Yang-Mills mathematical source tree in The Eriksson
  Programme: a pinned Lean 4 (v4.29.0-rc6) and Mathlib formalization of SU(N)
  lattice gauge theory foundations with a verified, zero-sorry, zero-axiom
  core (YangMillsCore, depending only on [propext, Classical.choice,
  Quot.sound]). Verified core results include the Kotecky-Preiss / Mayer
  polymer cluster-expansion engine, volume-uniform strong-coupling Wilson-loop
  area laws, unconditional IR exponential clustering for SU(N) without
  Peter-Weyl, fixed-spacing thermodynamic limits, SU(N)/U(1) Haar and center
  symmetry rules, Amos/Bessel ratio bounds, Z_2 reflection-positivity and
  transfer-operator chains, certified obstructions (volume-uniform Poincare
  walls, flat Hodge rank bounds), and source-grounded conditional
  renormalization-group interfaces. The physical hRpoly activity estimate
  (PR #29), 4D SU(N) reflection positivity/transfer, continuum limit (a -> 0),
  and Osterwalder-Schrader/Wightman reconstruction remain explicitly open.
keywords:
  - "Yang-Mills"
  - "lattice gauge theory"
